    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not retire the 30 AxReal axioms: `nat_axiom_inventory --include-constructed` still reports `real: axiom=30` and the Lean axiom ledger is still 30 of 30 real, because that ledger publishes what is DECLARED. This fact is about what is REACHED, and the gap between the two is now the whole of the trusted surface. Nor does it say the package is unused: LraReconstructCtx::try_new() still builds it in tests, in examples/front_door_carrier.rs and examples/ordered_ring_refutation.rs -- where it is the NEGATIVE CONTROL that keeps every axiom-freedom measurement in this repository from being vacuous -- and in the three relative-consistency models (Int, Rat, CReal), which are statements ABOUT the package and would be unstatable without it. Nor does it cover every public entry point: the fixtures drive prove_unsat_to_lean_module, and a route reachable only from some other entry point is outside what was measured. RENAMED 2026-08-19 (ADR-0522): the package's kernel declarations are now `AxReal`/`AxReal.*`, so this fact spells them that way. Nothing about the measurement moved -- `arith_prelude_builds()` counts calls to `build_arith_prelude`, not names, and every checker_command below is anchored on the counter line rather than on a declaration name.",
